---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = 'October 25, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use — Do Code That Matters"
  description="Terms of use for docodethatmatters.com."
>
  <main class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8 max-w-2xl">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Terms of Use</h1>

    <p class="mb-6 font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--color-text-muted);">
      Last updated: {updated}
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-6 font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--color-text-muted);">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">The site</h2>
        <p>
          This site (docodethatmatters.com, "Do Code That Matters") is a personal blog written and
          maintained by Spencer Kittleson. By using the site you agree to these terms. If you do not
          agree, do not use the site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">Content</h2>
        <p>
          The posts, code, and other content on this site are provided for general information and
          education. Code samples are shared so you can learn from them; reuse them in your own
          projects at your own discretion. Content linked to from this site is not mine, and I am not
          responsible for what third-party sites say or do.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">Use of the site</h2>
        <p>
          Please use the site the way a normal visitor would. Do not attempt to disrupt it, scrape it
          at scale, impersonate me or the site, or use it to send unsolicited messages through the
          contact form.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The site and its content are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. I do my best to
          keep things accurate, but code changes, products change, and I make mistakes. Nothing here
          is professional, legal, or financial advice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, I am not liable for any damages arising from your use
          of this site or reliance on its content.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">Changes</h2>
        <p>
          I may update these terms from time to time. The "last updated" date above reflects the most
          recent change. Continued use of the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms? Use the
          <a href="/about/" class="hover:underline" style="color: var(--color-accent);">contact form on the About page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
